WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.201
-Thank you very much!

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.703
Hello!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:07.707
And welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.108
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.644
Thank you for being here.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.447
Well, guys, big news
in Washington today as Congress

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:19.185 line:0%
finally passed the $1.9 trillion
COVID relief package.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:22.121
That's right!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:24.657
Most Americans are thrilled
the bill passed.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.694
In fact, President Biden is
so amped, he just bit his dog.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.396
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.331
That's right, this bill is huge.

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.267
It's $1.9 trillion.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.370
That's like a dollar for
every e-mail you got this year

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.539
that started with,
"in these challenging times."

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.807
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.576
Meanwhile, tomorrow,
President Biden will deliver

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.378
his first prime-time address

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.882
to mark the one-year anniversary
of the COVID shutdown.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.851
Yeah, one year ago today,
many Americans left

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.319
half a sandwich
in their office like,

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.389
"Eh, I'll get it tomorrow."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.957
Yep, Biden's very busy.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.326
Yesterday, he visited
a local hardware store

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.094
that received
a small-business loan.

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:03.529
And I thought his conversation

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.564
with the owners
was pretty interesting.

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:06.966
Take a look at this video.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:36.529
[ Laughter and applause ]
What?

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.332
Later in the conversation,
this happened.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:14.867
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:17.637
I just found it odd,
but then he left them with this.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:33.519
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.388
What's he talking about?

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.656
What?

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:39.959
Some business news here.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.062
I saw that 7-Eleven is adding
something new to its menu,

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:46.265
and judging by the reactions,
it should be a huge hit.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:50.036
-7-Eleven is adding a new item
to its hot-food lineup --

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.270
fish bites.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.940
-Fish bites.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.974
-I just think that's a bad idea.

00:02:55.974 --> 00:02:57.977
-I have a very sensitive
stomach, so I just get worried.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.178
I'm like, "Ooh, I don't know."

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:02.649
-I have never been one
to do fast-food fish.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.150
-This isn't even fast-food fish.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.752
This is 7-Eleven!

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:10.623
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.992
-When the fish bites were
added to the hot-food case,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:16.562
a 50-year-old taquito was like,
"Welcome to hell, bitch!"

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:22.435
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:25.204
I know they've been busy,
but how does the CDC

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.438
let this slip
through the cracks?

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:27.840
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.975
But this is nice.
If you order the fish bites,

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:32.145
they just automatically
hand you the bathroom key.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:36.549
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.818
Actually, I'd rather
eat the bathroom key.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.720
[ Laughter ]
Hey, well, this is cool.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.122
I saw that yesterday
Timbaland and Swizz Beatz

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:46.659
sold the streaming platform
Verzuz to Triller.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:49.362
I feel like that sentence
might be a little confusing

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.330
if you don't know
what those things are,

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.299
so here, let's test
that theory out.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.334
It's time for
"Tell a Grandparent."

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.136
♪ -Tell a grandparent ♪

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.805
-Now, we arranged for one of
our staff members' grandparents

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:01.941
to join us on Zoom
so we could tell them

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.977
the news and get their reaction.

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:06.145
Bob and Margaret, are you there?

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.281
-Hi, Jimmy.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.583
-Thank you for joining us today.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.652
Are you ready for your news?

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.087
-Sure.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:18.024
-Alright, yesterday,
Timbaland and Swizz Beatz

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:22.728
sold streaming platform Verzuz
to Triller.

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:24.897
-I'm sorry.
Could you repeat that?

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.165
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.366
-Sure.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:30.169
Timbaland and Swizz Beatz sold

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:33.773
streaming platform Verzuz
to Triller.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.441
-You think that's news?

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.578
Call us back when Jay-Z
sells Tidal to Clubhouse.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:46.085
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh!

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:49.856
-What? What?

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.925
I didn't --
That didn't go how I planned.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.460
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.896
Did they dab at the end?

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.765
Over in New Jersey,
I read about an Amtrak worker

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:02.067
who is being accused of stealing
some interesting equipment.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.369
Listen to this.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.137
-An Amtrak engineer
from New Jersey is accused of

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:09.976
stealing 77 chain saws,
103 chain-saw bars,

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:12.945
and 163 chains from Amtrak.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.547
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.316
-Luckily, he'll have no problem
in jail.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.983
They're like,
"What are you in for?"

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:19.919
"Stealing chain saws."

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:26.158
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.194
Every birthday, his wife
looks at her gift box like,

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:30.029
"Let me guess --
another chain saw."

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.297
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.732
"Put it in the closet
with the other ones."

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:36.768
And, finally, a lot of people
are talking about a TikTok

00:05:36.768 --> 00:05:39.939
that shows off one family's
DIY quarantine project.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.006
Watch this.

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:42.375
-During quarantine,

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.744
my husband built a video rental
store in our basement.

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:48.014
Instead of refinishing
our kitchen cabinets,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.017
he decided to build
a video rental store.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.686
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:56.155
-Meanwhile, their friends are
like, "I'm starting to think

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:58.257
that GoFundMe wasn't to help
with their mortgage."

